    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσπῐλ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		lit. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stainless</i>: hence,
				<i>faultless, without blemish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.1054c4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.252
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
				6.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Pet.</u>
				1.19
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἀπὸ παντὸς κινδύνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMag.Leid.V.</u>
					8.11
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			 vv. ll. for sq. in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.167
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσπιλος: χειμάρρους</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
